  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lagos State Employment Trust Fund (LSETF)-Regi Fit Garment Making Training Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With the arrival of the novel coronavirus, USADF and LSETF collaborated to conduct a Request for Proposals focused on healthcare services, infection control and sanitation, and PPE production. Regi Fashion School is proposing to provide pattern making training to 120 young Nigerians graduates resident in Lagos. Graduates from the Fashion school are highly sought after by garment making companies within and outside the country. The company is proposing to provide trainings in basic fashion designing.</narrative>
  </description>
